title: 'pallet-revive: count instantiation cost in the storage size integrity check'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The pallet's `integrity_test` checks that the storage a block can write fits the memory
    left to validators. Three things change in how it counts:

    - Immutable data: each stored value is charged one instantiation on top of
      `seal_set_immutable_data`. The result no longer depends on which machine benchmarked
      `seal_set_immutable_data`, so a hand-set weight for it can be replaced by the benchmarked
      one.
    - Regular storage: the term was close to zero before and now counts the items a block can
      write.
    - Events, storage and immutable data are counted by ref_time only.

    On asset-hub-westend the counted maximum drops from 179.9 MB to 30.1 MB of 201.3 MB.

    No migration is needed. If the integrity test of your runtime fails after this change,
    the block ref_time allows more storage writes than `(PVFMemory - RuntimeMemory) / 2`
    holds: raise `PVFMemory` or lower the block weight.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
